# Story 7.2 — large regenerable survey intermediate (embeds absolute audio paths;
# regenerate via `make non-rekordbox-survey`). The portable hash-keyed manifest +
# the two reviewable .md reports ARE committed.
_bmad-output/ml-training/non-rekordbox-survey.json

# Story 8.7 — large regenerable beat-grid artifacts (embed absolute audio paths;
# regenerate via `make oracle-generate-beats` / `make benchmark-beatgrid`, mirroring
# the un-committed daw-oracle.json). The small accuracy + downbeat report JSONs and
# 8-7-pressure-release.md ARE committed as evidence.
_bmad-output/ml-training/tony-corpus/rekordbox-beats.jams.json
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/8-7-estimated-beats.jams.json

# Story 7.3 — per-run ablation model artifacts. Only the large/regenerable ones
# are ignored: the model weights, the per-epoch log, and the run-B split sidecar.
# model_metadata.json IS committed (DD #8 forensic record). The harness (.py), the
# .md docs, and non-rekordbox-unsupervised-pretrain-manifest.json are committed;
# kdd-b2-comparison-v1.md is the operator-produced AC12 deliverable.
_bmad-output/ml-training/ablation/*/model.pt
_bmad-output/ml-training/ablation/*/model.pt.partial
_bmad-output/ml-training/ablation/*/training_log.json
_bmad-output/ml-training/ablation/*/run_b_random_split.json

# Epic 7 — substrate-v2 close-out. Regenerable: the Phase-1 smoke checkpoints, the
# operator-run FR-18 prediction dumps, and the large v2 training weights + logs.
# Committed: the per-seed model_metadata.json (forensic) + the eval .json/.md reports.
_bmad-output/ml-training/ablation/v2-smoke/
_bmad-output/ml-training/fr18-predictions/
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/*/seed_*/model.pt
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/*/seed_*/training_log.json
# Archived prior-model snapshots (feedback-archive-model-before-retrain): the small
# forensic files (FR18-RESULT.md, model_metadata.json, fr18-manifest.json,
# training_log.json) ARE committed for the attributable ladder; the heavy/regenerable
# binaries stay local-only (preserved on disk in _archive/, not bloating git).
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/_archive/*/model.pt
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/_archive/*/*.mlmodelc/
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/_archive/*/fr18-predictions.json
# Per-experiment FR-18 runtime prediction scratch dumps (regenerable via fr18-produce).
_bmad-output/ml-training/fr18-predictions-191/
# Stale earlier-corpus supervisedAugmented arm (different corpusVersionHash than the
# current maskedMelPretrain winner; not a matched FR-24 pair). Local-only scratch.
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/supervisedAugmented/
# Operator scratch logs at the v2-runs root (per-run console captures).
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/*.log
_bmad-output/ml-training/v2-runs/train-log.txt
# Per-seed experiment-iteration CoreML exports + their convert reports. These are
# regenerable from the (gitignored) seed checkpoints; only an authoritative,
# gate-passing model would be committed deliberately (as giantsteps_v2.mlmodel).
_bmad-output/ml-models/giantsteps_v2_seed_*.mlmodel/
_bmad-output/ml-models/giantsteps_v2_seed_*.mlmodelc/
_bmad-output/ml-models/giantsteps_v2_seed_*.convert_report.json

# Local review scratch output (NOT shipped)
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/review-tmp/

# Story 7.7 — the sealed GiantSteps holdout hash-list is LOCAL ONLY (smallest
# leak surface, DD #10). Only the committed giantsteps-holdout-v2-manifest.md
# (script ref + seed + SHA256 digest) is the reproducibility proof. Bare pattern
# (no leading slash) so it ignores at any depth.
giantsteps-holdout-v2.json
